  "body": "The `:stalled` pseudo-class and the `stalled` event share a name and are\nrelated, but have different conditions for matching/firing, which can cause\nconfusion for implementers and web authors.\n\nThis adds a note next to the `:stalled` declaration explaining that:\n- The pseudo-class is intended for displaying player state UI when playback\n  has been buffering for too long.\n- Unlike the `stalled` event (which fires on any network download stall\n  regardless of playback or ready state), `:stalled` additionally requires\n  the element to be currently buffering.\n\nAddresses https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12145#issuecomment-3882914935\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12174/semantics-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 4, 2026, 10:15 PM UTC (2a5164d)\">/semantics-other.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12174/ca2c39f...2a5164d/semantics-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 4, 2026, 10:15 PM UTC (2a5164d)\">diff</a> )",
